<title>USA: Del Webb to call senior notes, take loss.</title>
<headline>Del Webb to call senior notes, take loss.</headline>
<dateline>PHOENIX 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Del Webb Corp said it called all of its $100 million of 10 7/8 percent senior notes due 2000 for redemption on March 31 at par, resulting in a one-time loss of $0.07 per share.</p>
<p>The interest payment due March 31 would be paid in the usual manner, it said.</p>
<p>Redemption would result in a one-time extraordinary loss of $1.3 million or about $0.07 per share, from writing off unamortized issuance costs associated with the debt, the company said.</p>
<p>The loss would be reflected in the quarter ended March 31, the company said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
